// The S5 timer and counter rules of Siemens' STL and LAD manuals for the
// S7-300/400, one network each: SE and SS restart on a new edge while
// running, SS runs on when the start goes off, SF stops on a new start,
// SP and SD keep their time value when stopped, FR restarts a timer, a
// time value is truncated to its time base, and a counter set while CU is
// on counts in the next cycle; R of a counter works statically
tag Se Bool %I0.0
tag Ss Bool %I0.1
tag Sf Bool %I0.2
tag Sp Bool %I0.3
tag Sd Bool %I0.4
tag Fr Bool %I0.5
tag Rs Bool %I0.6
tag Cu Bool %I1.0
tag Cs Bool %I1.1
tag Cr Bool %I1.2
tag Qe Bool %Q0.0
tag Qs Bool %Q0.1
tag Qf Bool %Q0.2
tag Qp Bool %Q0.3
tag Qd Bool %Q0.4
tag Vp Word %MW10
tag Vd Word %MW12
tag Cv Word %MW14
tag Tv1 Word %MW16
tag Tv2 Word %MW18
tag Cv2 Word %MW20
A Se
L s5:1000
SE T 1
A T 1
= Qe
---
A Ss
L s5:1000
SS T 2
A Rs
R T 2
A T 2
= Qs
---
A Sf
L s5:1000
SF T 3
A T 3
= Qf
---
A Sp
L s5:1000
SP T 4
A T 4
= Qp
L T 4
T Vp
---
A Sd
L s5:1000
SD T 5
A Fr
FR T 5
A Rs
R T 5
A T 5
= Qd
L T 5
T Vd
---
L S5T#2S15MS
T Tv1
L S5T#2H46M30S
T Tv2
---
A Cu
CU C 1
A Cs
L c:5
S C 1
A Cr
R C 1
L C 1
T Cv
---
A Cs
L c:999
S C 2
A Cu
CU C 2
L C 2
T Cv2
